      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verdon%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was officially platted on February 22, 1882, marking its formal establishment.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verdon%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Missouri Pacific Railroad’s arrival in the early 1880s turned Verdon into a key shipping point for farm products.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/verdon_nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1906 the Farmers and Merchants Bank opened, followed in 1910 by the Maust Elevator, boosting local commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/verdon_nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Verdon sits near the site of a failed 1856 settlement called Springfield, which was abandoned after 26 years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
